	(descr "Panasonic AXK680137YG -- P5K series 0.5mm-pitch 80-pin board-to-board SOCKET, module side (confirmed on the ALINX AC7200 module; mates with the carrier board's own AXK680337YG header -- see ../../AC7200/AC7200_README.md). Real dimensions from Panasonic/Mouser's own P5K/P5KS catalog PDF (mouser.com/catalog/specsheets/AXK.pdf), read directly: body 23.20 x 19.50mm (A x B, same as the header), 0.5mm pitch, 40 pins/row x 2 rows staggered by 0.25mm (half pitch), pad 0.25 x 0.75mm, total footprint span 6.80mm (wider than the header's 5.60mm -- read directly off the Socket's own land-pattern drawing, not assumed equal to the header). CAVEAT, not silently resolved: the exact string 'AXK680137YG' (from the AC7200 module's own STEP model, AC7200.3.0.stp) does not decode cleanly against Panasonic's real P5K part-number table -- leading digit 6 is the Header selector, but mated-height digit 1 is documented as Socket-only. The catalog's real 80-contact/3.0mm bossed socket is AXK580137YG (one digit off, likely a typo in the STEP model's component name). Filed under the STEP file's literal name per the module's own reference data and the user's identification of it as the socket; dimensions above are real P5K Socket data either way, since both candidate part numbers are the same 80-contact/3.0mm-mated-height P5K socket. Pin numbering (1-80 sequential by row) is an ASSUMED convention, matching the header's own same assumption, not independently verified against a real pin-1 diagram.")
	(tags "Panasonic AXK680137YG P5K board-to-board 80pin 0.5mm socket")
